# tools/al/ales_stereo_expand_witness.rish -- stereo_expand: the downward expander carried into stereo, the gate's linked decision fused with the compressor's linked gain (ALES159).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus - the creative suite) - waymark ALES - rung ALES159.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-063651_fill-ales159-lotus-stereo-expand.md
# Stands on: lotus/expand.rye (ALES60 -- the mono downward expander, its expand and ExpandError reused whole for the louder-quiet-channel proof and the fault set), lotus/stereo_gate.rye (ALES156 -- the linked-decision law
# this fuses), lotus/stereo_compress.rye (ALES157 -- the linked-gain law this fuses), lotus/pan.rye (ALES10 -- the StereoClip and its balance invariant), lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 -- the Clip, sample_max).
#
# lotus/stereo_expand.rye expands a span of sample-PAIRS in a master below a magnitude threshold by a ratio, fusing a LINKED decision with a LINKED gain -- completing the core stereo dynamics quartet (gate - compressor -
# limiter - expander). The detector key per pair is max(|left|, |right|): at or above the threshold the pair passes byte for byte (continuous at the threshold); a both-silent pair stays zero; where the pair is below the
# threshold the widened master new_key = max(0, threshold − (threshold − key)-num/den) is computed once (exactly the mono expand of the louder channel) and BOTH channels are scaled by the single fraction new_key/key. It
# links the decision like the gate (a pair is expanded iff both channels are below the threshold) and the gain like the compressor (the widened factor is magnitude-dependent, so one gain from the linked key). ExpandError
# reused whole; the linked lift adds no fault. Values only, never a length. The crux is the linked decision + gain law (a pair expanded iff both below, the louder-quiet channel equal to the mono expand byte for byte, the
# quiet channel scaled by the same fraction, the independent lift differing), the image law (the shared gain preserves the L:R ratio, an out-of-phase quiet pair returning still out of phase), the at-threshold law (a pair
# whose linked key reaches the threshold passing byte for byte), and the knob laws (unit ratio the identity, a higher ratio harder, a huge ratio driving a quiet pair to silence -- the gate within).
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_stereo_expand_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-expand: Language EN — stereo_expand expands a span of sample-pairs in a stereo master below a magnitude threshold by a ratio, fusing a linked decision with a linked gain. For each pair the detector key is the max of the two channels' magnitudes: at or above the threshold the pair passes byte for byte, continuous at the threshold; a both-silent pair stays zero; where the pair is below the threshold the widened master new_key equals the max of zero and threshold minus the deficit (threshold minus key) times ratio_num over ratio_den, computed once exactly as the mono expander would for the louder channel, and both channels are scaled by the single fraction new_key over key. The louder-quiet channel lands on new_key, the quieter channel scaled by the identical fraction, so the left-to-right ratio is preserved. It validates threshold, ratio, and span once against the shared length before any write, so a refusal never expands one channel and leaves the other torn. It writes values only, never a length, so the two channels leave balanced; a both-silent pair stays silent and an empty span is a clean no-op on both."
say "ales-stereo-expand: Style Radiant — ALES60 named the mono downward expander: a sample at or above a magnitude threshold passes byte for byte, a sample below it has its deficit widened by a ratio and the sample rewritten sign(x) times the max of zero and threshold minus the widened deficit, the compressor mirrored under the threshold, deepening the quiet — the space between phrases opened wider, the room tone under a pause lowered, continuous at the threshold, the gate its hardest limit. Carried into stereo it fuses the two linking laws this family has proven. Its decision must be linked, like the gate: the expander pushes down the quiet, and expanding each channel by whether it alone is below threshold would push the quiet right down while the loud left plays — the image tears, exactly the gate's bug. So a pair is expanded only when both channels are below the threshold. Its gain must be linked, like the compressor: the widened factor is magnitude-dependent, so expanding each channel by its own deficit gives different gains and shifts the image. So the one gain is computed from the linked key and applied to both. The crux is five laws: the linked decision and gain law (a pair expanded iff both channels are below the threshold, both scaled by the same fraction, the louder-quiet channel equal to the mono expand byte for byte, the independent lift genuinely differing); the image law (the shared gain preserves the left-to-right ratio, an out-of-phase quiet pair returning still out of phase, no magnitude expanding and no sign flipping); the at-threshold law (a pair whose linked key reaches the threshold passing byte for byte on both, continuous at the threshold); the knob laws (unit ratio the identity everywhere, a higher ratio expanding at least as hard, a ratio far past the threshold driving a quiet pair to silence — the gate within); and the silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate law (a both-silent pair staying silent through the key-zero guard, length held, each refusal leaving both channels untouched and balanced, count zero and the empty span the identity on both)."
say "ales-stereo-expand: Lens TAME — two bounded in-process i16 Clips (left, right) expanded by one linked gain, one comparison of the linked key and at most one multiply-then-divide per channel per sample (in i64, the product of a magnitude and new_key at most 32768 times 32768 never overflowing), memoryless (no attack, hold, or release; those are later rungs); the two channels enter balanced (the StereoClip invariant asserted on entry) and leave balanced (an expander writes values only, each length asserted equal and within bound on exit); threshold, ratio, and span are validated once against the shared length before either channel is mutated, so a refusal never expands one channel and leaves the other torn; a both-silent pair is guarded by the key-equals-zero branch so no divide by zero can occur; StereoExpandError is ALES60's ExpandError (BadThreshold, BadRatio, BadRange) reused whole, the linked lift adding no fault. Nothing on the audio path can overflow: the widened result is floored at zero and new_key is at most key, so every scaled magnitude is at most its input's, which already fits i16. The linked decision and gain law is proven against a master where the left always holds the peak — the left equal to the mono expand of it byte for byte (500 to 0, 800 to 600, 2000 plays, 300 to 0) while the right is scaled by the same fraction (200 to 0, 400 to 300, 1500 plays, 100 to 0), and the independent lift (mono expand of the right alone, 400 to 0) shown to genuinely differ; the image law proves no magnitude expands and no sign flips over a mixed master and that an out-of-phase quiet pair returns still exactly out of phase (600, -200, 800, 0); the at-threshold law proves a master whose keys reach the threshold passes byte for byte on both; the knob laws prove unit ratio the identity everywhere, a higher ratio monotone, and a huge ratio driving a quiet pair to silence on both channels; and the silence, balance, atomicity, and degenerate cases prove an all-silent master staying zero, the length held, each of the four refusals leaving both channels untouched and balanced, and an empty span the identity on both; siloed to lotus/, the threshold a magnitude in sample units and the ratio a plain fraction, no real sample rate, no anti-aliasing, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_expand"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_expand.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-expand: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_expand.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-expand: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-expand: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-expand' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-expand: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-expand line"
